Instrument (nothing delivery-bound, nothing in patches/):
- LLAMA_KV_DEBUG_CELLS=1 / LLAMA_RS_DEBUG_CELLS=1 (WIP llama.cpp commit c49584c60): one compact line per ubatch
  for the KV cells (as runs), and the recurrent head/n/min/max/rs_z + per-cell pos/src/src0/tail, including the
  destination rows right after a seq_state_take().
- arms/two_arms.cpp: ARMS_LOGITS_DIR dumps every sampled row as raw f32 plus a sha256/argmax/top-5 manifest, so
  two arms' numerics can be diffed row by row.

Findings (RESULTS-2026-11-22.md, raw logs in runs/diag-cells-2611/ with compare.py):
- 2x2 on the hipBLASLt pin and the allocation state, full residency: the pin owns b79e73e3fe9f (with it the arms
  are bit-identical to the reference -- 480/480 logits rows, max|d| = 0 -- both requests, every rep), and the
  allocation state owns e05c6e16a136/abe253ea957a. The divergent row is R1's own PREFILL last row, so neither the
  take nor R1's recurrent tail is involved.
- The arms' KV cell census is identical to the single-context reference with one allocation state (0/243 lines,
  both shapes, every rep) and scatters without it (192/243: pos 512 lands in cell 0 while the prompt sits in
  512-1023) -- §3.4's two-cursor finding, measured directly, and T0's justification.
- On the product shape with BOTH pins the arms' warm text is still stably b79e73e3fe9f while batch-pair is stable
  at d5083bd41b4c, and the two runs' residency censuses differ (h=0.8161 vs 0.8172): a GREEDY-PURITY §89 residency
  class, so pass 1's 'the host tier is refuted' is itself refuted.
- Consequence: T3's strong oracle (a cross-configuration hash) IS available at full residency with the pin and one
  allocator; on the tier it is KLD + residency-class-matched text. ROCBLAS_USE_HIPBLASLT=0 is mandatory on every
  text arm, full residency included.
